From: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-usxgmii: avoid link-up reset in USXGMII mode

The PCS link-up callback reconfigures the USXGMII PCS and XFI PHY right
after phylink observes a successful in-band link. The line side stays
negotiated, but the MediaTek PCS carrier drops again, and since the next
link-up runs the same callback the port keeps flapping every one to two
seconds for as long as it is up.

USXGMII negotiates and reports its link state in band and the PCS has
already been configured before link-up, so do not tear that established
link down again. Keep the reconfiguration for the fixed-rate 5GBASE-R
and 10GBASE-R modes, and for a fixed 10G trunk to an external switch,
which has no in-band partner and does rely on it.

Backport of the 6.18 fix to the 6.12 PCS driver, where the callback is
an unconditional pcs_config() call. Reported against r11 on the GL-BE14000
10G WAN port, an RTL8261D in inband/usxgmii mode: link up at 1Gbps,
carrier down about a second later, repeating, with the correct PHY
driver bound and no resource exhaustion.

Signed-off-by: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
[backport to the 6.12 driver, keep fixed 10G trunks reconfiguring]
Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c
@@ -328,8 +328,21 @@ static void mtk_usxgmii_pcs_link_up(stru
 				    phy_interface_t interface,
 				    int speed, int duplex)
 {
+	struct mtk_usxgmii_pcs *mpcs = pcs_to_mtk_usxgmii_pcs(pcs);
+
+	/* USXGMII reports its link state in band and the PCS was already
+	 * configured before the link came up. Reconfiguring here only tears
+	 * down the established link, and as the next link-up calls this
+	 * again, the port flaps for as long as it is up. A fixed 10G trunk
+	 * to an external switch has no in-band partner and does need it.
+	 */
+	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII &&
+	    !of_property_read_bool(mpcs->dev->of_node,
+				   "mediatek,force-fixed-10g"))
+		return;
+
 	/* Reconfiguring USXGMII to ensure the quality of the RX signal
 	 * after the line side link up.
 	 */
 	mtk_usxgmii_pcs_config(pcs, neg_mode, interface, NULL, false);
 }
